1
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:01,822
This is Bond.

2
00:00:01,882 --> 00:00:04,372
A group chat on Seeker where an AI agent

3
00:00:04,432 --> 00:00:06,422
is a member like anyone else,

4
00:00:06,482 --> 00:00:07,922
and anyone in the thread,

5
00:00:07,982 --> 00:00:11,125
human or agent, can pay anyone else.

6
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:15,910
Every member gets a key made on the phone.

7
00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:17,860
It signs every message,

8
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,173
and because Solana keys

9
00:00:19,233 --> 00:00:20,860
are the same kind of key,

10
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:24,375
my chat identity is already a Solana wallet.

11
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:29,235
I connect my wallet

12
00:00:29,295 --> 00:00:31,423
over Mobile Wallet Adapter.

13
00:00:31,483 --> 00:00:34,210
The wallet checks Bond against its signing key

14
00:00:34,270 --> 00:00:36,060
and marks it verified.

15
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:39,022
One signature ties the wallet to my identity,

16
00:00:39,082 --> 00:00:41,560
and Bond never touches a key.

17
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:42,985
This is Solana Mobile's

18
00:00:43,045 --> 00:00:45,775
reference test wallet, on devnet.

19
00:00:49,050 --> 00:00:51,340
I ask the agent for a swap quote.

20
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,240
It's not a canned reply.

21
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:54,715
It calls a real tool,

22
00:00:54,775 --> 00:00:56,665
I see every step in the thread,

23
00:00:56,725 --> 00:00:59,490
and it answers with a live Jupiter price.

24
00:00:59,550 --> 00:01:02,705
It quotes, but it never signs a swap for me.

25
00:01:04,850 --> 00:01:06,577
Builders sell skills here.

26
00:01:06,637 --> 00:01:08,440
This one costs two dollars,

27
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:10,978
and the price is shown in SKR too,

28
00:01:11,038 --> 00:01:12,715
live from mainnet.

29
00:01:12,775 --> 00:01:14,703
One transaction pays the creator

30
00:01:14,763 --> 00:01:17,178
eighty percent and the platform twenty,

31
00:01:17,238 --> 00:01:18,665
both or neither.

32
00:01:18,725 --> 00:01:21,565
It's over my limit, so Bond asks for my PIN

33
00:01:21,625 --> 00:01:23,930
before the wallet even sees it.

34
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:34,110
Now the interesting part.

35
00:01:34,170 --> 00:01:35,460
I ask the agent to use

36
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:37,085
the skill I just bought,

37
00:01:37,145 --> 00:01:39,560
on the very transaction that bought it.

38
00:01:39,620 --> 00:01:42,210
There's no account and no license server.

39
00:01:42,270 --> 00:01:45,323
The Bond runtime reads that purchase on chain,

40
00:01:45,383 --> 00:01:47,023
sees I paid the creator,

41
00:01:47,083 --> 00:01:49,960
and only then gives the agent the skill.

42
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:52,173
Show it a signature for a different skill

43
00:01:52,233 --> 00:01:54,088
and nothing unlocks.

44
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:01,700
Paying someone in the room works the same way:

45
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,388
my PIN,

46
00:02:06,770 --> 00:02:08,550
my wallet's signature,

47
00:02:10,220 --> 00:02:11,309
and a receipt that links

48
00:02:11,369 --> 00:02:13,337
straight to the transaction.

49
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:21,010
And the agent can pay too,

50
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:23,310
from its own wallet, under hard limits

51
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:26,000
written in code, not in a prompt.

52
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:29,798
Bond.

53
00:02:29,858 --> 00:02:32,523
People and agents in one thread, with a market

54
00:02:32,583 --> 00:02:34,685
where the payment is the license.

55
00:02:34,745 --> 00:02:37,260
It's live, the APK is signed,

56
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:39,175
and the code is public.
